      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start, definitely professional. \n\nThat said, looking at the admin dashboard, the \"richness score\" for this draft came back a bit lower than I'd usually like to see for a flagship property. It's a little sparse in terms of the actual sensory details.\n\nCould you try another version? I really don't want you to just stuff adjectives in there for the sake of it—I'll reject anything that reads like a shopping list—but try to make it feel much more \"lush\" and evocative. Use more descriptive, colorful language to really paint the picture of the marble, the gardens, and the views so the score picks up a bit more, while still keeping that sophisticated Azure Coast Estates tone. Think more \"sensory experience\" rather than just \"features.\"",
